      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role"><strong>Process development</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Work">Improve yields and conditions</td>
          <td data-label="Rewarded for">Measured improvement</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role"><strong>Production and operations</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Work">Run batches</td>
          <td data-label="Rewarded for">Consistency and safety</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role"><strong>Quality control and assurance</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Work">Test and release</td>
          <td data-label="Rewarded for">Accuracy and records</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role"><strong>Research and development</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Work">Discover and test new routes</td>
          <td data-label="Rewarded for">Insight and method</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role"><strong>Technical sales and support</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Work">Explain products to customers</td>
          <td data-label="Rewarded for">Product knowledge and trust</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="batch">How to read a batch record, a core industry habit</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Part</th>
          <th>What it shows</th>
          <th>Why it matters</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Raw materials</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it shows">Names, amounts, lot numbers</td>
          <td data-label="Why it matters">Traceability</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Steps and times</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it shows">What was done and when</td>
          <td data-label="Why it matters">Repeatability</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Readings</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it shows">Temperature, pH and other measures</td>
          <td data-label="Why it matters">Quality and troubleshooting</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Deviations</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it shows">What went off plan and why</td>
          <td data-label="Why it matters">Learning and compliance</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Sign-offs</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it shows">Who checked each step</td>
          <td data-label="Why it matters">Accountability</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Practise by writing a clear record for a home kitchen process, such as fermenting dough, with times, amounts and observations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trouble">Troubleshooting thinking that plants reward</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Symptom</th>
          <th>Questions to ask first</th>
          <th>Likely area</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Symptom"><strong>Yield dropped</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Questions to ask first">Did raw material, time or temperature change?</td>
          <td data-label="Likely area">Inputs and conditions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Symptom"><strong>Product fails a test</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Questions to ask first">Which step differs from the last good batch?</td>
          <td data-label="Likely area">Process or measurement</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Symptom"><strong>Culture grows slowly</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Questions to ask first">Was the medium, pH or oxygen supply different?</td>
          <td data-label="Likely area">Growth conditions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Symptom"><strong>Foul smell or odd colour</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Questions to ask first">Was anything contaminated or left too long?</td>
          <td data-label="Likely area">Hygiene and timing</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Practise by comparing a good and a bad batch record line by line.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scale">Why scale-up is harder than it looks</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Factor</th>
          <th>At small scale</th>
          <th>At large scale</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Factor"><strong>Mixing</strong></td>
          <td data-label="At small scale">Easy and fast</td>
          <td data-label="At large scale">Slow and uneven</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Factor"><strong>Heat</strong></td>
          <td data-label="At small scale">Dissipates quickly</td>
          <td data-label="At large scale">Builds up and needs control</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Factor"><strong>Oxygen supply</strong></td>
          <td data-label="At small scale">Simple</td>
          <td data-label="At large scale">Needs design</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Factor"><strong>Cleaning</strong></td>
          <td data-label="At small scale">Quick</td>
          <td data-label="At large scale">Time-consuming and critical</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>

  <p>
    As a rule of thumb and not a research finding, keep a degree or course fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 8 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 80,000 for the main course, and a fifth is Rs 1.6 lakh as a serious caution. The rest can fund a laptop, practice time and a reserve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Test the field with free courses and one finished project before paying for a long programme. Do not borrow heavily for a course whose graduates cannot show placement in a specific role.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol for this career</h2>

  <p>
    Test the choice with <strong>The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</strong>: Biology, Context, Market and Survival.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Biology: do you like careful, repeatable work?</div>
        <p>Repeat a home recipe exactly twice and compare.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Context: time, money and home support</div>
        <p>Count study time, fees and support at home.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Market: who hires?</div>
        <p>Read ten notices for these roles and note the common skills.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
